The quick answer: skip the bits you don't find interesting.

This probably won't be good for the ascension chances of your current
character, but it should give you the chance to work out which
preparation steps you really *do* need.  If you wander around for long
enough pick-axeing Gehennom, accumulating potions and wands, then the
Run itself becomes less interesting.

I found that playing polyless/wishless made the late game more
interesting, in that I might have to attempt the ascension run with a
slightly less than complete Ascension Kit... but only until the point
that I started camping/farming to fill it out the long way.

(This is all from somebody who has difficulty ascending in <100k turns,
so listen to the faster ascenders first.)

